SensorHUD - Privacy Policy
Last updated: July 28, 2026

SensorHUD reads hardware performance information from the local Windows device
so it can display that information in an Xbox Game Bar widget.

Data handling

- Hardware readings and device names are processed locally on the device.
- The application does not transmit telemetry readings or device information
  to the developer or to third parties.
- The application does not contain advertising, analytics, user accounts, or
  cloud synchronization.
- Display preferences are stored only in the application's local package
  storage.

Hardware access

The application uses the signed PawnIO hardware-access driver for supported
low-level sensors. Its installer is included in the application package and is
run only when the required driver is missing, damaged, or outdated.

Questions

Privacy questions can be submitted through the issue tracker of the repository
that hosts this policy. Do not include private or sensitive information in a
public issue.
